# v1.13 P4 PR review — endorsement pass — REVISED after your blockers

This is the revised diff for the release-gate PR you reviewed (DO NOT SHIP YET, split: Claude CAUTION / Codex BLOCK, 5 items). Every item is addressed, plus one independent-finder MINOR and both of your "couldn't verify" test gaps. Confirm the blockers are cleared or name what still fails, with file:line. SHIP means mergeable — v1.13.0 tags after this.

## Your items → resolutions
1. **Run-card count name-axis (your #1):** the card now projects the reviser to a unique seat id (id-match first, else the same by_name collapse `choose_revision_seat` uses, so the projection matches the runtime pick on default duplicate boards) and counts `s.id != chosen_id`. `--board claude,claude,codex` prints "2 non-revision seat(s)"; tested both axes.
2. **Per-seat --timeout ignored (your #2):** the fan-out now mirrors the round precedence exactly (call-level override → seat.timeout_s → adapter cap); the `timeout=revision_seat.timeout_s` call parameter is gone. Test: a tiny per-seat `--timeout` drops exactly that endorsement seat (ABSTAIN/dropped) while the others vote.
3. **Egress wording (your #3):** rewritten at all four sites (runtime print, raw recorder, run card, prompt docstring) + the module docstring + one sentence in references/data-handling.md. New framing: "each is sent the source + the board-generated revised draft/changes under the run's existing disclosure (same category as round-2 review sharing; no new exposure class)" — with the explicit honesty clause that the revised draft is freshly generated here, not bytes the seat already received. No new consent gate (the category ruling you converged on: generated-derivative fan-out sits with round-2 review sharing).
4. **Revision-seat name-axis (your #4):** `--revision-seat` now resolves by unique seat id (`provider#N` on auto-numbered duplicate boards; bare names accepted only when unambiguous, ambiguous names refused listing candidate ids, matching the CLI's refusal voice). `changes.revision_seat`, revision artifact paths, and logs all record the id — on non-duplicate boards id == name, so every existing artifact stays byte-identical (verified). changes-schema.md documents the axis; CHANGELOG notes the user-facing change. Both duplicate seats individually selectable, tested.
5. **Endorsement-less byte-identity (your #5):** proven per the invariant of record (head CSS may evolve; the BODY must not — documented since P3): a new test renders an endorsement-less revised-draft run and asserts the `<body>` bytes are identical with the `{{ENDORSEMENT_SUMMARY}}` token stripped from the template entirely. Passed with zero residue, no behavior change needed.

## Your "couldn't verify" gaps, closed
- **Exotic OBJECT note byte-determinism:** new end-to-end test — a note with é and an embedded newline round-trips with sha256(changes.json on disk) == verdict.changes.sha256. It caught a real renderer bug: the multi-line note corrupted the summary `<li>`; fixed with the established `_flat` precedent (the per-seat .md keeps the note verbatim as the forensic record).
- **Duplicate-provider run-card projection and unique revision-seat selection:** both now directly tested (see 1 and 4).

## Also fixed (independent finder MINOR, consistent with your validator-strictness discipline)
`board_changes.validate` now enforces endorsement-target upper bounds (`edit_n <= len(edits)`, `unresolved_n <= len(unresolved)`) and refuses duplicate `(seat, kind, n)` rows — closing the standalone-validator gap against hand-authored files, matching the dense-`n` precedent the same validator already enforces for edits.

## State
Suite: **1279 OK** (+17 since your review's 1262; 1209 at the P3 baseline), verified by an independent full run. Write-order/sha coherence, concurrency byte-stability, parse atomicity, and escaping were verified clean by both you and the independent finder last round and are untouched except as described.

